# Cloudflare build output and local state.
#
# Not merely noise. `@opennextjs/cloudflare` inlines the resolved environment into
# `.open-next/cloudflare/next-env.mjs`, and with a Neon-linked `.env.local` that file contains a live
# `DATABASE_URL` — password and all. The directory was untracked but not ignored, so 34 files were
# stageable and `git add -A` would have committed a production database credential.
#
# The secret scanner caught it, which is the only reason this is a note rather than an incident.
.open-next/
.wrangler/
